{
  "_note": "Sector map locations (names: Logan, 2026-09-27; descriptions: Claude's drafts, approved by Logan 2026-10-13). Enemy pools use the roster in data/mechs (Claude's drafts to vet). Regular fights draw from `encounters` (Slay-the-Spire style, Logan 2026-09-28): the run's first few fights from `weak`, the rest from `strong`, weighted; three-enemy fights only come from `strong`. Compositions and weights are Proposed. Each visit to the sector map rolls a mission type per location (data/missions.json). On the War Table's theater map (WarMap, regenerated with each sector roll) `map_zone` places a location: coast (on the shore), flank (mountain foothills, an open-pit mine), backline (a mesa deep behind the enemy front); `map_icon` is its map glyph (anchor, pick, data). `modifiers` (Claude's drafts, 2026-09-30): rules always on at that location (data/conditions.json): rain at the Shipyard, jamming at the Data Archives, dust at the Mining Grounds. `local` (2026-11-19): the location's own enemies; the rest of its pools are roamers. Local ones are a little more likely (balance.json encounters.local_weight, at most about 20%), so roamers still show up. Shipyard pools rebuilt 2026-11-19 with its new enemies (Gaffhook, Kettle, Weldwright, Stevedore, Deck Gunner, Hull Ripper, Frogman; elites Pile Driver, Breakwater), mixing local and roaming fights. Mining Grounds pools rebuilt the same way 2026-11-19 (Crusher, Powder Monkey, Leacher, Shaftsinker, Dust Devil, Fuse, Mole; elites Excavator, Detonator). Data Archives pools rebuilt the same way 2026-11-20 (Firewall, Mimic, Coldline, Cable Rat, Watchdog, Redactor, Ghostnode; elites Archivist, Cryovault).",
